Cactus Code Thorn TestPersistentGroups
Author(s)    : Liwei Ji
Maintainer(s): Liwei Ji
Licence      : LGPL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Purpose

Test that refined-level coarse-fine ghosts of checkpointed grid functions
that the time integrator does not own are refreshed by SYNC under
subcycling. Both tested groups are checkpointed and not integrated, so both
are persistent and behave identically: persist_default carries only
checkpoint="yes", and persist_noevolve also carries a leftover evolve="no"
tag, which the driver ignores apart from a startup warning naming the group
(this group is the in-tree trigger for that warning). Each group holds a
time stamp written on the interior every step; a check counts the points
that hold neither the level's own stamp nor, on coarse-fine ghosts, the
parent level's stamp.

The tests run on top of TestSubcyclingMC2's RK4 evolution with a moving
refined box (regridded every 4 iterations): moving.par uninterrupted, and
checkpoint-moving.par / recover-moving.par as a checkpoint/recover pair with
a mid-cycle checkpoint between two regrids. After recovery the tested groups
are SYNCed and checked before evolution continues.
